 resulting Commercial Earnings; and
• the 50% amount payable to the Original Creator.

You must maintain reasonably sufficient records supporting those calculations for at least three (3) years.

Payment instructions shall be obtained from the Original Creator using the contact information stated at the beginning of this License.

Choosing Commercial Option A does not remove the source-code, copyleft, repository-link, or ordinary attribution requirements contained elsewhere in this License.

Commercial Option B — Prominent Commercial Attribution

Instead of paying the 50% amount described in Commercial Option A, You may choose Commercial Option B.

If You choose this option, the following notice must be displayed prominently:

“This commercial application is based on source code from [PROJECT NAME], originally created by ShadowOfPripyat. Revenue or profit generated by this application is made possible in part by source code from the original project.

Original source repository: https://github.com/ShadowOfPripyat/zip2apk”

For an Android application or other graphical application, this notice must appear:

1. in the application's About, Credits, Legal, or equivalent screen, where it can be accessed by an ordinary user without unreasonable difficulty; and

2. in the application's public store listing or official download-page description wherever the distributor controls such a description.

For a commercially distributed source-code project, library, command-line program, or other product without an application interface, the notice must instead appear prominently in its main README or equivalent introductory documentation and on its principal public distribution page.

The notice must be reasonably legible and may not be deliberately hidden, minimized, obscured, or placed only in source files that ordinary users would not normally see.

The wording may be translated into another language, but the translation must preserve the meaning of the notice and the Original Repository link must remain intact.

Choosing Commercial Option B means that no revenue payment under Commercial Option A is required, provided that all requirements of Commercial Option B and the remainder of this License are continuously satisfied.

